          "_name": "article08",
          "_sourceTheme": "startm5",
          "_customHTML": "<section class=\"zl-page\">\n<div class=\"zl-wrap\">\n<nav class=\"zl-crumbs\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><ol><li><a href=\"index.html\">Home</a></li><li aria-current=\"page\">Terms of Use</li></ol></nav>\n<h1>Terms of Use</h1>\n<div class=\"zl-card zl-body\"><h2>1. General information, not legal advice</h2>\n<p>The content of this website is general information for families from Ukraine in Germany. It does not replace legal, medical or tax advice. Rules and procedures change and differ between authorities. Always check the official sources we link to.</p>\n<h2>2. Voluntary support</h2>\n<p>ZusammenLeben is a volunteer initiative. Support is free of charge and depends on our capacity at the time. There is no right to a specific service, apartment, appointment or result. Decisions about benefits, residence and school places are made by the responsible authorities.</p>\n<h2>3. External links</h2>\n<p>We link to official and trusted websites. We have no influence on their content and are not responsible for it. If you notice a broken or problematic link, please tell us.</p>\n<h2>4. Copyright</h2>\n<p>Texts, graphics and photos on this website are protected. You may share links to our pages freely. Copying content requires our permission.</p>\n<h2>5. Contact</h2>\n<p>Questions about these terms: <a href=\"mailto:zusammenleben.de@gmail.com\">zusammenleben.de@gmail.com</a>.</p>\n<p><em>Last updated: October 2026.</em></p></div>\n</div>\n</section>",
